# Frontend unit tests

Specs live in `frontend/tests/unit/`, named `<subject>.spec.ts`, run with `npm test` from `frontend/`.

## Layers

- NGXS → `tests/unit/state/` (follow `tasks.state.spec.ts`)
- helper / pipe / service → `tests/unit/helpers/`, `pipes/`, `services/`
- component template → `tests/unit/components/`

## Component specs

A cheap first-stage net: if AI deletes a title, a button, an `@if` block, or a `data-test` hook, Jest should fail in seconds — before Playwright.

Select with `[data-test="..."]` or user-visible text. Do not select by CSS class. Do not assert spacing, tokens, or `should create`.

Canonical tripwires:

- `tests/unit/components/task-tile.component.spec.ts` — title binding and `@if` menu
- `tests/unit/components/home-sync-status.component.spec.ts` — banner copy and Sync now
- `tests/unit/components/home-bottom-panel.component.spec.ts` — create button and nav hooks
- `tests/unit/components/task-side-menu-item.component.spec.ts` — label from input

A screen flow still gets Playwright. Component spec does not replace e2e. Pure logic still belongs in a helper spec, not the component spec.
